│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compact_shared_cube_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the dense per-qubit, line-entangled block with a much more             │
│                          │ parameter-efficient symmetric ansatz that previously showed stronger validation/test      │
│                          │ behavior on this task family.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new block uses:                                                                       │
│                          │ - one shared input RY mixer across all qubits,                                            │
│                          │ - a 3-matching cube-style CZ entangler that better matches the fixed binary feature map’s │
│                          │ multi-qubit correlations,                                                                 │
│                          │ - a shared RY/RX output mixer to convert phase information into Z-readout signal.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Dramatically fewer trainable parameters per block, improving parameter efficiency and   │
│                          │ lowering overfitting risk.                                                                │
│                          │ - More balanced entanglement than a simple line, which is better aligned with the feature │
│                          │ map’s pairwise couplings.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Shared parameters encourage smoother optimization and faster convergence under Adam.    │
│                          │ - This structure is consistent with the best-performing prior candidate on the same task, │
│                          │ which achieved better validation/test accuracy and a smaller train-test gap than the      │
│                          │ current over-parameterized block.                                                         │
