│                          │ still be underusing non-diagonal entanglement.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My revised block keeps the same parameter budget as the current program, but changes the  │
│                          │ internal structure to improve phase-to-amplitude conversion and gradient flow:            │
│                          │ - preserves symmetry with shared parameters across qubits,                                │
│                          │ - replaces one of the purely diagonal sections with a non-diagonal CRY bridge,            │
│                          │ - keeps three complementary entangling matchings for broad connectivity,                  │
│                          │ - maintains a compact 4-parameter-per-block design, so the total parameter count stays    │
│                          │ efficient.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help validation/test accuracy and reduce the train-test gap without           │
│                          │ increasing model size.                                                                    │
